ort":true,"mirror_uv":false,"isOpen":false,"locked":false,"visibility":true,"autouv":0,"rotation":[0,0,0],"children":[]}]}],"textures":[{"path":"elf_walkway.png","name":"elf_walkway.png","folder":"","namespace":"","id":"0","width":64,"height":256,"uv_width":64,"uv_height":256,"particle":false,"use_as_default":true,"layers_enabled":false,"sync_to_project":"","render_mode":"default","render_sides":"auto","frame_time":1,"frame_order_type":"loop","frame_order":"","frame_interpolate":false,"visible":true,"internal":true,"saved":true,"uuid":"b82cda2d-9ca6-58a0-bde1-d3c181405482","relative_path":"elf_walkway.png","source":"data:image/png;base64,"}],"animations":[],"description":"# elf_walkway\n\nElf walkway segment: a raised wooden walkway on posts, 4 columns long along Z, deck 120 u up, curved rails built from stepped pale wood. Segments join end to end; slot_walk_a / slot_walk_b mark the joins.\n\n- Footprint: 1 x 4 columns (16 x 64 units, 0.45 x 1.80 m), centred on the origin, front (door side) faces -Z.\n- Finished bounds: x -8..8, y 0..138, z -32..32 units.\n- Texture: 64 x 256, 1 px per unit, square pixels, nearest filtering. Every visible face has its own texture region painted with its material at world position (seams line up across faces); identical faces share a region; construction and ruined pieces map into the region of the face they were cut from. No cube is cut to fit the texture.\n- Cubes: finished 29, construction_0 6, construction_33 6, construction_66 19, ruined 7 (0 rotated: roof slabs and a few leaning props).\n\n## Hit box\n\n- deck: 16 x 4 x 64 at y 118..122 (walkable on top); posts 3 x 118 x 3\n\n## State group sets (children of `root`; show exactly one)\n\n- `finished`: the finished building (visible by default).\n- `construction_0`, `construction_33`, `construction_66`: build progress at 0 %, 33 % and 66 % (staked outline and scaffold, then walls rising inside scaffold, then full frame with roof rafters).\n- `ruined`: collapsed shell, broken walls, rubble, fallen roof (use with `_damaged.png`, or `_abandoned.png` for F7 abandoned buildings).\n- `elf_walkway_damaged.png`: damaged texture (scorch, holes, cracks) for the same UVs; works on every group set.\n- `elf_walkway_abandoned.png`: abandoned look (damage plus moss, faded cloth, cold fires) = `abandoned_elf_walkway` together with the `ruined` set or the finished set.\n\n## Attachment and effect points (empty groups)\n\n- `slot_walk_a` at (0, 122, -32)\n- `slot_walk_b` at (0, 122, 32)\n"}